wildos-setup (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * When saved passwords could not open by themselves, a notification says
    so once per boot and opens Settings at the fix: an account signing in
    automatically with no key kept (turned on before keys were kept), or a
    wallet whose password is not the account's.
  * wildos-wallet-keys checks the caller's own password (CheckPassword).

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000

wildos-setup (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * wildos-wallet-keys changes an account's own password (ChangePassword):
    it checks the current password, then runs the passwd PAM stack as root
    with the account as the real user, so the password rules apply. passwd
    has no setuid on Wild OS, so Settings could not change passwords.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000

wildos-setup (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * An account that signs in automatically gets its saved passwords too:
    wildos-wallet-keys keeps the key that opens its KWallet, readable by
    root only, and wildos-setup-wallet opens the wallet with it at each
    start. Setup keeps the key when it turns automatic sign-in on.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

